-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner laws ascend along an extension of constants
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ ($p$ prime), $N$ a nonzero natural number, $H'$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, and $\ell$ a prime coprime to $N$, with $N$ and $\ell$ nonzero in $K$; let $\kappa$ be a field equipped with an algebra map to $K$. Write $\Gamma_{H'}(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ for the preimage of $H'$ under the lower-right-entry character of $\Gamma_0(N)$, and, for a field $F$, write $F(\Gamma)$ for the subfield [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of $F((q))$ generated over $F$ by the quotients of reductions to $F$ of integral power series that are $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ modular forms on $\Gamma$ (denominator having nonzero reduction). Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeBetaModLHDefined`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L143) over $\kappa$ and over $K$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ carries $F(\Gamma_{H'}(N))$ into $F(\Gamma_{H'}(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell))$ for $F = \kappa, K$; then `heckeBetaModLH` is that substitution, while `heckeAlphaModLH` is the inclusion of $F(\Gamma_{H'}(N))$ into $F(\Gamma_{H'}(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell))$. Let $\rho_\kappa$, $\rho_K$ be monoid homomorphisms from $\Gamma_0(N)$ to the $\kappa$- resp. $K$-algebra automorphisms of $F(\Gamma_{H'}(N))$ satisfying `IsDiamondPullbackModL`, the pull-back law sending a ratio $p_{f_1}/p_{g_1}$ of reductions of integral $q$-expansions of $f\mid_k\gamma$, $g\mid_k\gamma$ to $p_f/p_g$. Suppose $W_\kappa$ is a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism of $\kappa(\Gamma_{H'}(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell))$ satisfying four laws: $W_\kappa(\alpha x) = \beta x$ and $W_\kappa(\beta x) = \alpha x$ for all $x$ whose Laurent series lies in the subfield $\kappa(j, j_N)$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`; $W_\kappa(\alpha x) = \beta(\rho_\kappa(\gamma)x)$ for all $x$, where $\gamma$ is a chosen element of $\Gamma_0(N)$ with lower-right entry the inverse of $\ell$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$; and $W_\kappa(\beta x) = \alpha x$ for all $x$. Then there exists a $K$-algebra automorphism $W_K$ of $K(\Gamma_{H'}(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell))$ satisfying the same four laws over $K$, with $\rho_K$ in place of $\rho_\kappa$.
--
--   This is the ascent, along an extension $\kappa \to K$ of the field of constants, of the Atkin–Lehner involution together with its compatibilities with the two degeneracy maps and with the diamond action on the mod-$\ell$ function field of $X_{H'}(N) \cap X_0(N\ell)$. It is used to pass from the case $\kappa = \overline{\mathbb{F}}_p$ to an arbitrary algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ in the construction of the Atkin–Lehner automorphism with these properties.
